`opentelemetry-sdk`: `RandomIdGenerator` now draws trace and span IDs from operating-system entropy (`secrets`) instead of the global `random` generator, so `random.seed()` in application code no longer makes separate processes or restarts deterministically repeat IDs, and forked workers no longer inherit identical generator state (issue #4376). IDs are consequently no longer reproducible via `random.seed()`; pass a custom `IdGenerator` to `TracerProvider` if you need deterministic IDs
